================================================================================
PREAMBLE
================================================================================

ChiptuneSynth is a source-sealed, freely distributable audio synthesis library
developed and owned exclusively by 8Binami SAS ("8Binami", "the Licensor").

"Source-sealed" means the distributed files are compiled and obfuscated to
protect the underlying intellectual property, while remaining free to use,
embed, and ship in your projects under the terms below.

This license governs all use of the ChiptuneSynth software, its compiled
output, documentation, and associated materials (collectively, "the Software").

By downloading, installing, or using the Software, you agree to be bound by
the terms of this license. If you do not agree, do not use the Software.


================================================================================
TIER 0 — FREE LICENSE (Non-Commercial & Indie)
================================================================================

The Software may be used at no charge, subject to ALL of the following
conditions:

1. ELIGIBLE USE. Free use is permitted exclusively for:

   a) NON-COMMERCIAL projects that generate zero revenue:
      - Personal projects, experiments, and learning
      - Educational and academic work (students, teachers, institutions)
      - Game jams and hackathons, including prize-winning entries
      - Portfolio projects and public demonstrations
      - Internal prototypes and proof-of-concept work

   b) INDIE commercial projects where the total gross annual revenue
      across ALL products using the Software is below $100,000 USD (or
      equivalent in any currency, calculated at the date of measurement).

      Revenue is measured across the licensee's entire business entity,
      not per-product. Once this threshold is exceeded, a paid license
      (Tier 1 or above) is required within 30 days.

2. ATTRIBUTION REQUIRED. All projects using the Free License must display
   the following attribution in a clearly visible location (credits screen,
   about page, game description, README, or in-app notice):

       "Audio powered by ChiptuneSynth — 8Binami.com"

   Attribution must be human-readable and reasonably prominent. It may not
   be hidden, obfuscated, or placed exclusively in source code comments
   for end-user-facing releases.

3. SINGLE ENTITY. The Free License is granted to a single individual or
   organization and may not be shared across separate legal entities.

4. DISTRIBUTION. You may ship the Software embedded in your product to
   end users (players, visitors, customers) without restriction.
   See Section "DISTRIBUTION & SUBLICENSING" for full terms.

5. NO REVERSE ENGINEERING. Decompiling, deobfuscating, disassembling, or
   attempting to reconstruct the source code of the Software in any form is
   strictly prohibited.

6. NO TAMPERING. You may not modify, patch, or tamper with the obfuscated
   distributed files. Extension through the documented public API is
   permitted and encouraged.

7. GAME JAM TO COMMERCIAL. Free use is permitted for game jam submissions.
   If a submission is subsequently commercialized, the $100,000/year revenue
   threshold applies from the date commercial revenue begins.


================================================================================
TIER 0-OSS — OPEN SOURCE EXCEPTION
================================================================================

Projects released under an OSI-approved open source license and meeting ALL
of the following criteria qualify for the Open Source Exception:

   - Publicly hosted (GitHub, GitLab, or equivalent)
   - Source code openly available under an OSI-approved license
   - Not directly monetized (no paid downloads, no paywalled features)
     Note: accepting donations does not disqualify a project.

Rights granted under Tier 0-OSS:

   - All Tier 0 rights
   - Attribution is OPTIONAL — no credit required
   - Unlimited contributors within the project

To claim this exception, include a note in your project's README referencing
this license clause. No registration required.


