================================================================================
DISTRIBUTION & SUBLICENSING
================================================================================

END-USER DISTRIBUTION (all tiers):
   You may embed and ship the Software within your finished product to
   end users — players, visitors, subscribers, or customers — without
   restriction and without requiring those end users to obtain a separate
   license. This covers games, web applications, mobile apps, and SaaS
   products.

DEVELOPER REDISTRIBUTION (not permitted without OEM license):
   You may NOT redistribute the Software as a standalone library, SDK,
   plugin, or as part of a game engine, framework, middleware, or
   developer tool — whether free or commercial — without a separate
   OEM license from 8Binami. Contact licensing@8binami.com.

CLIENT WORK:
   Agencies and freelancers may use the Software in work delivered to
   clients. The license covers the licensee (the agency/freelancer),
   not the client. Clients receiving a finished product are considered
   end users and do not require a separate license.


================================================================================
CONTINUITY GUARANTEE
================================================================================

8Binami is committed to the long-term availability of ChiptuneSynth.
In the event that 8Binami SAS ceases operations or permanently
discontinues ChiptuneSynth:

1. All perpetual license holders (Tiers 1–3) are automatically granted
   an irrevocable, royalty-free, worldwide license to continue using the
   version(s) they have licensed, for the lifetime of their existing
   products, with no further obligation to 8Binami.

2. The last stable release of each major version will be deposited with
   a trusted third-party escrow service. Enterprise clients may request
   source code escrow under a separate escrow agreement.

3. Annual license holders retain usage rights for the duration of their
   last paid term. No automatic renewal obligation arises.

This guarantee does not grant rights to new versions, updates, or
support beyond what was included in the original license.


================================================================================
LICENSE VERIFICATION & ENFORCEMENT
================================================================================

1. SELF-REPORTING. Revenue tiers operate on an honor system. 8Binami
   reserves the right to request reasonable revenue verification (e.g.,
   platform dashboards, financial filings) for accounts suspected of
   tier misrepresentation.

2. AUDIT RIGHT. 8Binami may audit compliance with 7 days written notice,
   once per calendar year per licensee. Audits are conducted via document
   review; no access to internal systems is required.

3. GRACE PERIOD. Licensees have 30 days from the date their revenue
   exceeds their current tier to upgrade. No retroactive fees are charged
   within the grace period if the licensee upgrades within this window.

4. TERMINATION. 8Binami may terminate any license immediately and without
   refund upon:
      - Material breach of this license
      - Attempted reverse engineering of the Software
      - Persistent non-payment after 30-day written notice
      - Deliberate misrepresentation of revenue tier

   Upon termination, the licensee must cease all use of the Software and
   remove it from all active products within 30 days.
   Perpetual license holders in good standing retain rights under the
   Continuity Guarantee above.

5. LICENSE TRANSFER. Licenses are not transferable to a different legal
   entity (e.g., upon acquisition or merger) without prior written consent
   from 8Binami. Transfer requests will be evaluated within 15 business
   days. Reasonable transfer fees may apply for Tier 1 and Tier 2.

6. REFUND POLICY. Annual licenses are refundable within 14 days of
   purchase if the Software has not been used in a released product.
   Perpetual licenses are non-refundable after 30 days.


